  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127908,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 343,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Almost all lesions arise in the lower extremities {30930084; 32362008}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:03:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127909,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 343,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with asymptomatic, slowly growing, erythematous or violaceous scaly plaques varying in size between 20&nbsp;and 70&nbsp;mm that are often described as poikilodermatous. The plaques are typically solitary, rarely multiple. Although clinically the lesions raise concern for poikilodermatous mycosis fungoides, on histology these two entities share no common features.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:03:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127910,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 343,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most of the patients are elderly men.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:03:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
